# Testing Strategy

Defines the minimum testing structure for the reusable app foundation.

## Mandatory rules

- Must use `flutter_test` for unit and widget tests.
- Must use `integration_test` for startup, navigation, and important flows.
- Must use `patrol` (via `patrol_test/`) for end-to-end module workspace flows.
- Should use `mocktail` or provider overrides for repository/data-source tests.
- Should keep tests close to source structure where practical.
- Must test controllers, value objects, mappers, validators, and shared components.
- Must test responsive behavior for important shared layouts and page shells.
- For UI sync changes, must test local success patching, cancel/failure behavior, typed delta or targeted refresh, event-group membership, and reconnect refresh.
- Cross-stack shared mutations must have backend event-emission coverage and a simulated peer-client reconciliation test.
- Tests must not depend on real production services or require secrets.

## Test types

| Test type | Target |
|---|---|
| Unit | validators, mappers, use cases, value objects |
| Widget | components, pages, responsive layout, forms |
| Integration | startup, routing, auth shell, platform flows |
| Patrol E2E | workspace shells, cross-module navigation |
| Golden | optional, for stable shared UI only |

## Acceptance checklist

- `flutter test` passes.
- Important components have widget tests.
- Providers can be overridden in tests.

